      "text": "among you: and my soul shall not abhor you, Lev. 26:11. All my inward friends abhorred me, Job 19:19. Wherefore I abhor myself, Job 42:6. Lord will abhor the bloody and deceitful man, Ps. 5:6. He deviseth mischief … he abhorreth not evil, Ps. 36:4. heard this, he was wroth, and greatly abhorred Israel, Ps. 78:59. thou hast cast off and abhorred … thine anointed, Ps. 89:38. insomuch that he abhorred his own inheritance, Ps. 106:40. the people curse, nations shall abhor him, Prov. 24:24. the land that thou abhorrest shall be forsaken, Isa. 7:16. they shall be an abhorring unto all flesh, Isa. 66:24. Do not abhor us, for thy name’s sake, Jer. 14:21. they abhor him that speaketh uprightly, Amos 5:10.",
